   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to the provision of records upon the receipt of a complaint\nof an incident of abuse or neglect of an individual with a disability",
    "basePrintNo": "S7024",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7024-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Executive",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7024          Revised 5/25/2021\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to the provision of records upon the receipt of a\ncomplaint of an incident of abuse or neglect of an individual with a\ndisability\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to improve access to records and facilities\nfor the independent agency that has been established as the Protection\nand Advocacy System (P&A) to conduct an investigation.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would authorize the independent agency to have prompt access\nto records or data of a facility or access to a facility upon the\nreceipt of a complaint of an incident of abuse or neglect, or in\ninstances related to an investigation of a violation against the rights\nof an individual with a disability who resides in a facility and is\nreceiving services and supports at such facility.\n\nThe independent agency would also be able to receive copies of records\nupon written request free of charge within three days or if there is a\ncomplaint of health or safety that puts an individual in serious and\njeopardy, or in the case of death of an individual with a disability,\nwithin twenty hours of receipt of a written request. Further, records\nmust be provided electronically at the request of the independent agen-\ncy.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe broad ability to obtain records and have access to physical\nlocations by New York State's Protection and Advocacy System (P&A) is\nessential to ensure transparency and expose abuse, neglect, and rights\nviolations of people with disabilities. As New York's P&A, one of Disa-\nbility Rights New York's (DRNY) most critical functions is to investi-\ngate allegations of abuse and neglect of people with disabilities in the\nlocations where they receive services.  Federal law gives the P&A system\nbroad access to records promptly - typically one to three business days.\nNevertheless, DRNY continues to be met with refusals and delays. For\nexample, the Department of Corrections and Community Supervision (DOCCS)\nhas implemented onerous prerequisites for obtaining copies of records.\nDOCCS requires DRNY to schedule an appointment to travel to any of New\nYork's 52 correctional facilities, physically select pages of records,\nwait to receive an invoice, and prepay by check before DOCCS will\nprovide copies. This result in months of delay well beyond the lawful\ntimeline has expired.\n\nThese requirements have completely prevented DRNY from obtaining records\nduring COVID-19. DOCCS has even refused to make an exception to its\nin-person review requirement during the pandemic. DOCCS appears to be\ntaking these actions for the sole purpose of preventing DRNY from exer-\ncising its P&A mandates.\n\nDRNY's investigations of the impact of COVID-19 on people with disabili-\nties in group homes and other congregate settings have also been thwart-\ned. DRNY had to resort to the Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) for\naccess to data regarding deaths and infection rates in group homes\nduring the pandemic. The Office for People with Developmental Disabili-\nties (OPWDD) then used a loophole in FOIL to refuse to provide this data\nsought for seven months which prevented DRNY and the public of informa-\ntion essential to developing effective response measures in real time.\nDRNY has also encountered resistance from private, state-licensed, agen-\ncies who are unfamiliar with the P&A or who falsely believe that they\nare exempt from the federal P&A laws. These scenarios illustrate the\nneed to clarify and strengthen the P & A authority.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is new Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nUndetermined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
